# Siya visuals — slide-by-slide approval gate

When a prompt asks for a **carousel or static image** (Siya Health brand creative), do
**not** produce the full pack in one pass. Follow this order:

## Phase 1 — copy plan only (cheap to change)

1. Research (if evidence-based) + draft the on-frame copy deck in chat or `copy/carousel.md`.
2. No captions, no video prompts, no tracker rows, no WorkDrive sync yet.

## Phase 2 — one image at a time

1. Generate the **first slide only** (photo + composited render).
2. Show it in chat and run the self-audit (face-safe, blur-test type, CTA ship gate,
   correct theme/template, **A-03 lean lock**: headline + sub-headline only unless
   `--dense` was explicitly requested).
3. **Wait for user approval in chat** before rendering the next slide.
4. Repeat slide by slide. Batch later slides only if the user says the style is locked
   (e.g. "rest look good, continue").

## Phase 3 — ship only after approval

Only after the user approves the final slide set:

- Write captions (5 platforms + ALL-PLATFORMS)
- Write video prompt docs (pack + `07-Video-Prompts/`)
- Add tracker row (git CSV + WorkDrive)
- Sync pack to WorkDrive `05-Carousels/[ID]/`

## Why

Rework is image-heavy and expensive; captions/trackers/sync built against unapproved
visuals get thrown away. The approval checkpoint lives **in chat with the user** — the
automated ship gates (CTA overflow, face-safe crop) do not replace it.

## Scope

Applies to `apps/siya-health/brand/` creative work (editorial packs, statics, carousels).
Does not change the Vercel/staff-portal deploy rules.

**A-03 lean lock:** see `.cursor/rules/siya-a03-lean-lock.mdc` and
`apps/siya-health/brand/VISUAL-OS-TEMPLATES.md` → A-03.
